all right it's time for audience  questions after a breaker of a couple of  weeks I've got some really good ones  this week and that we've been on fire  with these audience questions lately  just a lot of good ones coming in first  one is from surah who said hey how do  you guys handle people who start telling  you way too much about themselves or  their problems or just won't stop  talking to you so I'll sort of talk  focus on the first part because I've  talked I think the last time we did  audience questions there was a question  about how to get out of a conversation  that you don't want to be in or  something and I said at a business event  I will just ask for someone's card and  then that'll interrupt the conversation  while they grab the card and then I  immediately say nice to meet you and  then it's a good opportunity to walk  away in social situations it can be a  little tougher but I've had people who  are sort of like a too much information  type of thing and the thing is  culturally like in the u.s. it's seen as  weirder so after meeting someone briefly  to go into more detailed things about  your personal life health issues for  example or family problems  in Argentina where I was born it's way  more common that you're just talking to  the clerk at a clothing store and they  might start talking to you about a  health issue that they're having or  whatever so I think it's all sort of but  there's some arbitrary nature to it in  terms of what's expected in a particular  culture but I have experience for me the  problem isn't hearing about personal  things from people it's about where  there's really an expectation that we're  gonna have like a ten-second exchange  and then it just seems to go on and on  and on where the other person thinks  it's okay to just just kind of like be  having a conversation when it's not  really the right setting for it I will  usually just pull out my phone and  nobody really knows whether the phone  has vibrated or not right though even  though you didn't hear a ring the phone  might have vibrated so I'll just pull it  out and I'll put a finger up and say oh  you know I'm sorry I'm gonna have to  deal with this and then I can just step  away and very rarely will anyone be  offended by that and it's sort of a  victimless lie I find depends on the  situation but I often expect them to ask  for money at some certain point like if  you're in a city in your approached by  someone yeah and they start going on  this long spiel about how they have to  buy a train ticket to get home to the  significant other okay yes expects  alright they're obviously going to ask  for money at some point how do I get out  of this conversation before they waste  all that time doing that right but  that's like we're more specific in a in  a panhandling type situation you never  know when it's gonna be a panhandling  situation or not or you don't like it  could just want to talk let's assume  you're at a social gathering right and  you've been just introduced to someone  new and your mutual friend has walked  away to get a drink at the bar area or  something like that and you're left with  someone who goes you know it's really  tough but I've been having this  persistent rash and it's the weirdest  thing because I've taken benadryl and it  doesn't seem to be an allergic thing and  I've not been been bitten by any animal  or anything like that and it's just  every morning I get up and I you know I  shower and I do my thing and the rash  just keeps getting worse and worse and  you know what and I actually I would go  see a doctor but the thing is I don't  actually have health insurance right now  and you know it  it cost me 25 dollars that's when I  start to get skeptical that's when I  start thinking that they're going to try  to ask for money yeah well but I guess  the idea is if it's a social event what  do you do excuse yourself to the  bathroom I just try to not along I guess  and deal with it I mean I'm pretty blunt  about those sorts of things where I'll  just you know make clear that I want to  change the topic of conversation yeah or  that I'm just not it really interested  because clearly they're over sharing I  know people who say in these situations  they just say nothing wit because they  say listen if you don't engage in the  conversation the other person will stop  talking not true there are people who  will just continue they'll continue  talking even if you say nothing and  those who say hey that person was a  really good listener so I think it's  okay I think it's a victimless deception  to either say excuse me I have to visit  the restroom or pretend that your phone  just buzzed and that you've got to deal  with something on the phone I don't see  any problem with that it just seems like  if someone opens up a conversation with  you meeting you for the first time yeah  with a topic that's so personal to them  and something that would obviously  perturb you in some way or form they're  just not worth having in your network  you can see what I mean  they just don't seem to have the best  social skills one of the things that has  changed for me from my early 20s into my  mid to late 20s and then into my early  30s is in my early in mid 20s I was much  more willing to sort of continue to  associate and be around people and  relate to people that I didn't really  enjoy being around because I felt that  you know it's good to have the largest  possible network of people you're in  touch with or you know it's just if that  person is seen as cool or popular then I  should try to align myself with them at  whatever cost there is I don't care  about that anymore I have done  everything I can to sort of rid my  personal network of people that I find  to be either toxic or just not enjoyable  to be around because you know what life  is short and why am i bothering you know  what why why why tolerate it well you  say you get out you ask for business  cards to get out of those awkward  situations in a professional setting and  then it goes rash maybe just ask for a  phone number oh I do the same thing in a  personal I'd love to follow up - can you  give me your phone number I think it  would go to hear about that rash I was  that yeah tell me about the rash be a  text please

